dule:MDBT50Q-512K","kicadFootprint":"RF_Module:Raytac_MDBT50Q","kicad":{"officialSymbol":{"ref":"RF_Module:MDBT50Q-512K","url":"https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/kicad%2Flibraries%2Fkicad-symbols/repository/files/RF_Module.kicad_symdir%2FMDBT50Q-512K.kicad_sym/raw?ref=45efbd93be87e365a21d743daf9b8a07e6414df6"},"officialFootprint":{"ref":"RF_Module:Raytac_MDBT50Q","url":"https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/kicad%2Flibraries%2Fkicad-footprints/repository/files/RF_Module.pretty%2FRaytac_MDBT50Q.kicad_mod/raw?ref=a0dcd398e7ea4b00cdeb91efc35f09cceaa9097d"},"footprintNote":"MODULE-61: use the official/vendor footprint","pinout":true},"buy":[{"store":"LCSC","url":"https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C6904155.html","priceUsd":8.8},{"store":"DigiKey","url":"https://www.digikey.com/en/products/result?keywords=MDBT50Q-512K"},{"store":"Mouser","url":"https://www.mouser.com/c/?q=MDBT50Q-512K"},{"store":"JLCPCB parts","url":"https://jlcpcb.com/parts/componentSearch?searchTxt=C6904155"},{"store":"Octopart","url":"https://octopart.com/search?q=MDBT50Q-512K"}]}],"released":2019,"status":"active","datasheetUrl":"https://docs.nordicsemi.com/bundle/ps_nrf52833/page/keyfeatures_html5.html","productUrl":"https://www.nordicsemi.com/Products/nRF52833","notes":["Serial sharing: SPIM0/TWIM0 and SPIM1/TWIM1 share hardware; SPIM2, SPIM3 (32 MHz) and both UARTEs are separate. Max is 4 SPI, or 2 I2C + 2 SPI + 2 UART at once.","USB 2.0 Full-Speed is device-only (no host).","VDDH accepts 2.5-5.5 V (e.g. USB VBUS or Li-ion). In that mode the REG0 output that feeds VDD/GPIO defaults to 1.8 V; set UICR REGOUT0 to get 3.3 V I/O.","The QFN40 package brings out only 18 GPIOs. The aQFN73 has 42 but needs fine-pitch PCB rules (via-in-pad/0.5 mm inner rows).","No ROM bootloader; flash over SWD. The micro:bit v2 uses an interface MCU for drag-and-drop flashing.","Not an official Matter target in nRF Connect SDK (use nRF52840/nRF5340/nRF54L15). MicroPython runs on the micro:bit v2 through the separate micro:bit port, not upstream ports/nrf.","Arduino support comes through community cores (e.g. arduino-nRF5 for the micro:bit v2)."],"sources":["https://docs.nordicsemi.com/bundle/ps_nrf52833/page/keyfeatures_html5.html","https://www.nordicsemi.com/Products/nRF52833","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C2895249.html","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C504799.html","https://github.com/adafruit/circuitpython/tree/main/ports/nordic/boards","https://github.com/platformio/platform-nordicnrf52/tree/develop/boards"],"boards":["microbit-v2"]}